# Formatting target for the Havel C++ tree.
#
# This config describes the TARGET style, not the current tree: measured
# against the existing sources, a full pass changes 10-93% of lines
# depending on the file, because the tree mixes 2-space (havel-lang
# compiler/vm/gc/stdlib) and 4-space (core/, tools/, parts of VM.hpp)
# populations, plus tabs in 51 files. Adopt INCREMENTALLY:
#
#   - format a file only when you are already touching it for real work,
#     or in a formatting-only commit for that file
#   - never bulk-reformat: it destroys git blame on the hot files and
#     wedges in-flight work; use `git blame -w` to survive the churn
#   - do not reformat files under active investigation mid-bisect
#
# Base: LLVM (2-space indent) — the dominant style of the largest
# subsystem (src/havel-lang/ compiler+vm+gc+stdlib, where all language
# work happens). Verified smallest-diff there: GC.hpp 10%,
# BytecodeIR.hpp 25%, TimeModule.cpp 32% under this config.
---
BasedOnStyle: LLVM
ColumnLimit: 100
PointerAlignment: Right
SortIncludes: Never
IncludeBlocks: Preserve
CompactNamespaces: true
# The tree's closing comments vary (`// close havel::compiler`,
# `// namespace havel::compiler`); rewriting them is pure noise.
FixNamespaceComments: false
AllowShortFunctionsOnASingleLine: Inline
KeepEmptyLinesAtTheStartOfBlocks: false
